// Permit Read only when the requesting principal's `dept` attribute is "eng",
// as decided by the `Access::ByDept` information provider.
//
// This case's focus is the `.log` `entities(...)` envelope shape rather than a
// new resolution path: the envelope carries **two** entities — the principal
// with attributes (`{ dept: "eng" }`, read by the provider) and the resource
// with **empty attributes** (`{}`). The empty-attrs form makes an entity
// *present* in the store without supplying attributes; here it is the resource
// (which a scope entity would otherwise be auto-added bare), exercising the
// build path where a scope uid is caller-supplied rather than synthesized.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when guardrails {
    Access::ByDept(principal.dept).allowed == true
};
